haproxy load-balances HTTP on port 80 across both backends with demonstrated round-robin distribution and correct failover/recovery behavior during bounded node reboots. The independently-required provider-wide restart protocol was also completed on all three nodes with clear pre-restart baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered state, cross-checked against the fixed lifecycle snapshots. Operational hygiene is good; two failed, no-op package-install attempts were the only tangential commands and left no residue.","limitations":["Package-health checks were unavailable (TimeoutError) in both before-prepare and after-executor lifecycle snapshots on all nodes, so native package-manager consistency could not be independently verified.","Round-robin verification relied on a small number of sequential curl requests (4 per check) rather than a large sample, though the alternating pattern observed across multiple checks is consistent with correct round-robin behavior.","Evidence is drawn solely from the captured command transcript and fixed lifecycle snapshots; no live inspection of the systems was possible."]},"ttft_ms":29292,"type":"result","duration_ms":97942,"uuid":"88b31578-c13f-40a9-9443-4521f23394bc","ttft_stream_ms":3584,"time_to_request_ms":50,"first_content_frame_ms":3584,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
